From 51d39816d5299650d3bfc836da6aec3b82f36e16 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: PyScotch <pyscotch@noreply.invalid>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 09:27:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 179/240] Bugfix: select the partitioning objective from
 `options[METIS_OPTION_OBJTYPE]` [report R. Perry]

The MeTiS v5 graph partitioning routines chose between edge cut and
communication volume according to whether a `vsize` array was
provided, and ignored `options[METIS_OPTION_OBJTYPE]`. Hence, callers
asking for `METIS_OBJTYPE_VOL` without vertex sizes received an edge
cut, while callers providing vertex sizes with the default objective
received a communication volume, as `METIS_PartMeshDual()` already
honored this option.

The objective is now read from the option array: edge cut uses the
edge loads and ignores vertex sizes, communication volume uses the
vertex sizes, unit sizes being assumed when none are provided.

Refs: CLI-19
